<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-UKRAINE BEAT ALBANIA 1-0.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-UKRAINE BEAT ALBANIA 1-0.</headline>
<dateline>GRANADA, Spain 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine beat Albania 1-0</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0) in their group nine World Cup qualifying match on</p>
<p>Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Serguei Rebrov 39</p>
<p>Attendance: 250  (two hundred and fifty)</p>
<p>Albania: 1-Foto Strakosha 2-Ghergji Dema (15-Altin Haxhi</p>
<p>46th minute), 3-Fatos Daja 4-Eduard Abazaj 5-Rudi Vata</p>
<p>6-Salvator Kacaj 7-Kliton Bozgo (17-Alban Bujhaj 73rd) 8-Artan</p>
<p>Bellai (13-Zamir Jhpuza 81st) 9-Bledar Kola 10-Altin Rraklli</p>
<p>11-Fatmir Vata</p>
<p>Ukraine: 1-Oleg Suslov 2-Mikhail Starostyak 3-Serguei</p>
<p>Bejenar 4-Alexandr Golovko 5-Vladislav Vachtchuk 6-Dmitro</p>
<p>Myhaiylenko (16-Vassili Kardach 71th) 7-Gennadiy Orbu 8-Youri</p>
<p>Kalitvintsev (15-Valeriy Kriventsov 85th) 9-Vitali Kossovskii</p>
<p>10-Andriy Shevchenko 11-Serguei Rebrov.</p>
<p> Standings	  </p>
<p>			  P   W   D   L   F   A  Pts    </p>
<p> Portugal	     6   2   3   1   5   2   9</p>
<p> Ukraine		4   3   0   1   4   2   9</p>
<p> Northern Ireland   5   1   3   1   4   3   6</p>
<p> Germany		3   1   2   0   6   2   5</p>
<p> Armenia		4   0   3   1   3   7   3</p>
<p> Albania		4   0   1   3   1   7   1</p>
